<title>UK: TransCo UK gas forecasts for February 22.</title>
<headline>TransCo UK gas forecasts for February 22.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>TransCo, the pipeline arm of BG plc, has announced the following forecasts and data for gas use in the period February 20-22.</p>
<p>DEMAND:</p>
<p>(mcm = million cubic metres)</p>
<p>Feb 20 (actual) 301 mcm, 70 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>Feb 21 (forecast) 277 mcm, 65 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>Feb 22 (forecast) 258 mcm, 60 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>TEMPERATURE:</p>
<p>20 Feb (actual) 8.9 Celsius, seasonal normal 4.6 Celsius</p>
<p>21 Feb (forecast) 9.6 Celsius, seasonal normal 4.7 Celsius</p>
<p>22 Feb (forecast) 9.1 Celsius, seasonal normal 4.7 Celsius</p>
<p>There was no interruption on February 21, and TransCo says the probability of interruption on Saturday 22 is low in every Local Distribution Zone.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom, +44 171 542 6412</p>
</text>
